    {
      "id": "5f836f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "See the University Catalog for the full listing of degree requirements for this major. See the Admissions website for transfer admission requirements &amp; Admissions deadlines See approved General Education courses at CSU Fullerton. See Associate Degree for Transfer. See the Credit by Exam information (AP, IB, CLEP) .",
      "contentHtml": "<blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See the </span><a href=\"https://catalog.fullerton.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">University Catalog</a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"> for the full listing of degree requirements for this major. </span></blockquote><blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See the Admissions website for </span><a href=\"https://admissions.fullerton.edu/prospectivestudent/transferlocaladmissionarea.php\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">transfer admission requirements</a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"> &amp; </span><a href=\"https://admissions.fullerton.edu/deadlines/index.php\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Admissions deadlines</a></blockquote><blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See </span><a href=\"https://www.fullerton.edu/undergraduate/general-education/approved-courses.html#box5\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">approved General Education </a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">courses at CSU Fullerton. </span></blockquote><blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See </span><a href=\"https://www.calstate.edu/apply/transfer/Pages/associate-degree-for-transfer-major-and-campus-search.aspx\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Associate Degree for Transfer.</a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"> </span></blockquote><blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See the </span><a href=\"https://registrar.fullerton.edu/articulation-tc/artic-agreements/external-exams/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Credit by Exam information (AP, IB, CLEP)</a><a href=\"https://www.calstate.edu/attend/student-services/casper/Pages/external-exam-credit.aspx\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">.</a></blockquote>"
    },
    {
      "id": "fd7f6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "About This Major",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "03806f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "(120 UNITS) The Bachelor of Arts in Public Administration ( Link ) prepares students for service in public agencies or nonprofit organizations. Students study the larger political environment of public service and the concepts and goals that underline such functions as budgeting, personnel, policy analysis and management. Specifically, the curriculum provides opportunities for students to develop an understanding of factual knowledge about the role and function of the public and nonprofit sectors of society, including: understanding the role of the administrative function in political system; the role of personnel administration, public budgeting and finance in creating and implementing public policy; the role of public administration professionals as participants in creating and implementing public policy; and different models of politics and governance as they relate to the role of administrative agencies and processes, particularly their role in democratic systems. The program prepares students for employment in government. In addition to the requirements for the major, students must meet all other university requirements for a bachelor’s degree. Please consult the Graduation Requirements for the Bachelor’s Degree section in this catalog for complete information.",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong>(120 UNITS)</strong></p><p>The Bachelor of Arts in Public Administration (<a href=\"https://catalog.fullerton.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=101&amp;poid=47439&amp;returnto=15150\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a>) prepares students for service in public agencies or nonprofit organizations. Students study the larger political environment of public service and the concepts and goals that underline such functions as budgeting, personnel, policy analysis and management. Specifically, the curriculum provides opportunities for students to develop an understanding of&nbsp;factual knowledge about the role and function of the public and nonprofit sectors of society, including: understanding the role of the administrative function in political system; the role of personnel administration, public budgeting and finance in creating and implementing public policy; the role of public administration professionals as participants in creating and implementing public policy; and different models of politics and governance as they relate to the role of administrative agencies and processes, particularly their role in democratic systems. The program prepares students for employment in government.</p><p><br></p><p>In addition to the requirements for the major, students must meet all other university requirements for a bachelor’s degree. Please consult the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://catalog.fullerton.edu/content.php?catoid=101&amp;navoid=15099\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Graduation Requirements for the Bachelor’s Degree</a>&nbsp;section in this catalog for complete information.</p><p><br></p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "ff7f6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 4,
      "content": "Transfer Success Pathway major eligible",
      "contentHtml": "<p><a href=\"https://www.calstate.edu/apply/transfer/Pages/transfer-success-pathway.aspx\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Transfer Success Pathway</a> major eligible </p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "b8a730af-af06-4545-b0d0-019d68d6b5af",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 5,
      "content": "The information provided here is subject to change without notice. Please be advised that articulation agreements published here may be updated or added at any time. Be sure to check with a counselor or adviser for the most current requirements. For additional transfer information: For C-ID information: https://c-idsystem.org/courses/ For Common Course Numbering: https://registrar.fullerton.edu/articulation-tc/artic-agreements/common-course-numbering/",
      "contentHtml": "<p></p><p></p><p><strong><em>The&nbsp;information&nbsp;provided&nbsp;here&nbsp;is&nbsp;subject&nbsp;to&nbsp;change&nbsp;without&nbsp;notice.&nbsp;Please&nbsp;be&nbsp;advised&nbsp;that&nbsp;articulation&nbsp;agreements&nbsp;published&nbsp;here&nbsp;may&nbsp;be&nbsp;updated&nbsp;or&nbsp;added&nbsp;at&nbsp;any&nbsp;time.&nbsp;Be&nbsp;sure&nbsp;to&nbsp;check&nbsp;with&nbsp;a&nbsp;counselor&nbsp;or&nbsp;adviser&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;most&nbsp;current&nbsp;requirements.&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p></p><p></p><p><strong>For&nbsp;additional&nbsp;transfer&nbsp;information:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>For&nbsp;C-ID&nbsp;information:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://c-idsystem.org/courses/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://c-idsystem.org/courses/</a></li><li>For&nbsp;Common&nbsp;Course&nbsp;Numbering:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://registrar.fullerton.edu/articulation-tc/artic-agreements/common-course-numbering/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://registrar.fullerton.edu/articulation-tc/artic-agreements/common-course-numbering/</a></li></ul>"
